      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Modern guidelines from organizations like the American Diabetes Association no longer treat older medications as a strict one-size-fits-all starting point for type 2 diabetes. Instead of relying solely on metformin, choice between an SGLT2 inhibitor and a GLP-1 receptor agonist as a first-line or early therapy depends heavily on individual health goals, organ protection needs, and patient preference.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
